1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,608
Before a first client meeting, I spend a couple of hours reading about
the company.

2
00:00:08,458 --> 00:00:10,122
This does the gathering for me,

3
00:00:10,972 --> 00:00:12,999
and every line it writes has a source.

4
00:00:13,849 --> 00:00:18,030
It's a simulated engagement, and it only reads public web pages.

5
00:00:18,625 --> 00:00:20,609
Here's a saved brief for Club Med.

6
00:00:21,459 --> 00:00:25,256
A planner wrote six questions, researchers searched the web for each,

7
00:00:26,106 --> 00:00:28,410
and a critic in plain code checked the work.

8
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:31,266
Forty-one findings made it through.

9
00:00:31,859 --> 00:00:33,843
Every line cites a numbered source.

10
00:00:34,693 --> 00:00:36,933
For each source, it went back to the page

11
00:00:37,783 --> 00:00:39,596
and checked the quote is really there:

12
00:00:40,446 --> 00:00:42,302
thirty-two of thirty-seven here.

13
00:00:42,921 --> 00:00:44,734
Then ten questions for the meeting,

14
00:00:45,584 --> 00:00:48,443
three use-case guesses with what we don't know yet,

15
00:00:49,293 --> 00:00:51,469
and a short email asking for a call.

16
00:00:53,078 --> 00:00:54,614
I can ask about the brief.

17
00:00:55,464 --> 00:00:57,405
What do guests complain about most?

18
00:00:58,255 --> 00:01:01,178
It answers only from the findings, with their IDs.

19
00:01:02,028 --> 00:01:03,223
No new searches.

20
00:01:03,828 --> 00:01:06,772
A live brief costs about fourteen cents in searches,

21
00:01:07,622 --> 00:01:10,886
so without a demo code there are three a day for everyone,

22
00:01:11,736 --> 00:01:14,467
and all live runs stop at ten dollars a month.

23
00:01:15,062 --> 00:01:18,475
In the eval, seventeen of eighteen briefs pass every check.

24
00:01:19,325 --> 00:01:21,437
The weak spot is made-up companies:

25
00:01:22,287 --> 00:01:25,615
on the held-out ones it stayed honest in only one of three.

26
00:01:26,465 --> 00:01:28,321
That's written down, not hidden.

27
00:01:28,937 --> 00:01:31,625
It's live, the link's below, and so is the code.
